# Workspace layout

This repo is a Go 1.27 workspace (`go.work`) with a root module `github.com/lordnynex/mcp`. Each top-level directory except `lib/` is one MCP server package: `github.com/lordnynex/mcp/<name>`. Run `go test ./...` from the repo root. Add a nested workspace module only when a library needs its own go.mod.

- Put importable server logic in `package <name>` at the module root.
- Export `New() *mcp.Server` and `Register(*mcp.Server)` so servers run standalone or mount into an aggregate.
- `cmd/<name>/` is a Cobra CLI. `main.go` only executes the root command. Do not put importable logic in `package main`.
- Shared code lives under `lib/` workspace modules. Process logging uses `lib/logger`.
- Never use an `internal/` directory. See [no-internal.mdc](no-internal.mdc).
- Unit tests use gest.

```go
// ✅ GOOD — library package, mountable
func New() *mcp.Server {
    s := mcp.NewServer(&mcp.Implementation{Name: Name, Version: Version}, nil)
    Register(s)
    return s
}

// ❌ BAD — tools only exist in package main; cannot be mounted later
func main() {
    s := mcp.NewServer(...)
    mcp.AddTool(s, ...)
}
```
